{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Aaron and his sons.</b> His sons' sons are included in \"his sons.\" \"You shall appoint them\" — to give an assignment to each one. And they shall guard their priesthood, so they do not come to disqualifications." "<b>And the stranger who draws near.</b> To a priest, to be among their priesthood — whether an Israelite or a Levite — <b>shall be put to death.</b> And the section \"And I, behold, I have taken\" is also joined, for there are in the Torah sections joined in meaning, and if they are set apart [they are so] like \"And it came to pass, when all the men of war had finished\"; so too \"And it came to pass on the day that YHWH spoke to Moses.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:04.250244883Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}